WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.100
The answer to check seven: no.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.400
Once on, purge protection can't be
turned off, and that's the point.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.263
Scene eight.

4
00:00:07.263 --> 00:00:12.172
The portal's WAF tuning runs under a
waiver that expires on December first,

5
00:00:12.172 --> 00:00:14.988
so the kit warns it's
due within thirty days.

6
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:19.683
A week later, the platform team switches
the gateway's firewall to prevention,

7
00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:23.719
adds the west origin's header, routes
the web subnet to the firewall,

8
00:00:23.719 --> 00:00:26.213
and turns on the vault's purge protection.

9
00:00:26.213 --> 00:00:30.024
A new address arrives, with
no owner and no protection.

10
00:00:30.024 --> 00:00:32.849
The kit compares the two
weeks by fingerprint,

11
00:00:32.849 --> 00:00:36.564
and records each run as evidence
that supports the controls,

12
00:00:36.564 --> 00:00:40.850
with its key security indicators,
its hashes and the record before it.
